    - Upload

Structure
    Orchestrator
        Calculates the reference orbit (several frames ahead) and broadcasts to renderers
        Assigns encoders a segment
        Assigns frames to renderers, along with the information of its segment's encoder
    Rendering Pool (Workers)
        Receives frames and computes its viewport (ideally does this while the GPU is busy)
        Computes pixel data of that viewport on the GPU
        Sends the raw data to the associated encoder for that segment
        Notifies the orchestrator when it is ready for another assignment
    Encoding Pool (Workers)
        Receives raw frame data encodes it for local storage
        When it has all frames, encodes frames into a video segment
        Saves video segments to shared storage
        Notifies the orchestrator when it is ready for another assignment
